A||N||5||johnt671||6 month old MSD coil died, What should I check.||||5||
Z||000000||johnt671||09-14-2001||08:21 PM|||| About 6 months ago I put an MSD blaster GM coil # 8226 on my 84.  Yesterday it died.  Is there something I should check before I toast another coil.  The car has an MSD 6A  system on it and I did the plugs, wires (Accel 8mm) cap and rotor (both heavy duty).  The car was running great and just died at about 50 mph.  I bypassed the 6a to make sure it wasn't that and put a cheap coil in and the car started right up.  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rick 88||09-14-2001||09:09 PM||||John,<P>MSD has a tech line you can call 8-5 (MST) at (915)855-7123 or you can e-mail you questions to msdtech@msdignition.com .<BR>You may have a defective unit. MSD is very good about help and replacement parts.<P>Hope this helps,<P>Rick<BR>yellow 88 GT 5-speed||||reg||1
